name 'ai-and-algorithmic-decisions-postassessment-q1_2026'

question 'A bookstore site shows a small "Quick View" panel when you hover over a book cover. Some users say the panel pops up when they didn''t mean to look at it. What change would best improve user-centered design?'

wrong 'Make the Quick View panel appear faster.'
right 'Change the trigger so the panel only appears when the user clearly chooses to see it, such as on click instead of hover.'
wrong 'Add more books to each row so the panel is harder to trigger.'
wrong 'Hide the panel entirely and let users open each book in a new tab.'

allow_multiple_attempts true

